  "question": {
    "text": "In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>YDSE</mi></math>, the slits have different widths. As a result, the amplitude of waves from two slits is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>A</mi></math> respectively. If <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> be the maximum intensity of the interference pattern then the intensity of the pattern at a point where the phase difference between waves is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ϕ</mi></math> is given by <math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math> . Where P is in&nbsp; integer. Find the value of P?",
    "image": null
  },
